<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33381" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paestum</span></b> , i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of
			Lucania</i>, <i>formerly called</i> Posidonia, <i>celebrated for its twice-blowing roses</i>, now <i>Pesti</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">biferique rosaria Paesti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 119</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 708</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 5, 5,
				61</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppidum Paestum Graecis Posidonia appellatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 10, § 71</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paestānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pœstum</i>, <i>Pœstan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 16, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rosae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 2, 4, 28</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paestāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Pœstans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
